# Tests for the Interest module

Run with `clerk test`. Numbers are worked out by hand from
`catala/interest.catala_en` and checked against Direct File where an oracle
scenario exists (`catala/tests/oracle_interest.catala_en`).

> Using Interest
> Using Types

## Helper: a report with only box 1 filled in

```catala
declaration scope Box1Report:
  input amount content money
  output report content Interest.InterestReport

scope Box1Report:
  definition report equals
    Interest.InterestReport {
      -- filer: Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler
      -- has_1099: true
      -- no_1099_amount: $0
      -- writable_1099_amount: amount
      -- writable_early_withdrawl_penalty_amount: $0
      -- writable_interest_on_government_bonds: $0
      -- writable_tax_withheld: $0
      -- writable_foreign_tax_paid: $0
      -- writable_tax_exempt_interest: $0
      -- writable_specified_private_activity_bond_interest: $0
      -- writable_market_discount: $0
      -- writable_bond_premium: $0
      -- writable_bond_premium_on_treasury_obligations: $0
      -- writable_bond_premium_on_tax_exempt_bond: $0
      -- state_is_different_state: false
      -- writable_state_tax_withheld: $0
      -- facta_filing_required: false
    }
```

## Schedule B threshold and the rounding branch

Three reports of $500.49, $500.49 and $499.02 total exactly $1,500.00, which
is not over $1,500: no Schedule B, so line 2b is the exact sum rounded once.
The per-item rounded amounts ($500, $500, $499) would give $1,499 instead.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestTotal1500NoScheduleBRoundsRawSum:
  output ok condition
  r1 scope Box1Report
  r2 scope Box1Report
  r3 scope Box1Report
  i scope Interest.Interest

scope TestTotal1500NoScheduleBRoundsRawSum:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition r1.amount equals $500.49
  definition r2.amount equals $500.49
  definition r3.amount equals $499.02
  definition i.interest_reports equals [r1.report; r2.report; r3.report]
  definition i.has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts equals false
  definition i.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition i.agi equals $0
  definition i.flow_has_seen_deductions equals false
  assertion not i.requires_schedule_b
  assertion i.interest_income = $1,500
  # the per-item branch would have given $1,499
  assertion i.interest_income != $1,499
  assertion not i.unsupported
```

Three reports of $500.51 total $1,501.53, which is over $1,500: Schedule B,
so line 2b is the sum of the per-item rounded amounts, $501 each, $1,503.
Rounding the raw sum once would give $1,502 (the quirk Q-R1 difference).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestTotal1501ScheduleBSumsPerItemRounded:
  output ok condition
  r1 scope Box1Report
  r2 scope Box1Report
  r3 scope Box1Report
  i scope Interest.Interest

scope TestTotal1501ScheduleBSumsPerItemRounded:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition r1.amount equals $500.51
  definition r2.amount equals $500.51
  definition r3.amount equals $500.51
  definition i.interest_reports equals [r1.report; r2.report; r3.report]
  definition i.has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts equals false
  definition i.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition i.agi equals $0
  definition i.flow_has_seen_deductions equals false
  assertion i.requires_schedule_b
  assertion i.interest_income = $1,503
  # known-bad outputs are rejected: the raw-sum rounding and the raw sum
  assertion i.interest_income != $1,502
  assertion i.interest_income != $1,501.53
```

Foreign accounts or trusts require Schedule B whatever the amount: $10 of
interest, Schedule B required, line 2b $10.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestForeignAccountsWith10RequiresScheduleB:
  output ok condition
  r1 scope Box1Report
  i scope Interest.Interest

scope TestForeignAccountsWith10RequiresScheduleB:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition r1.amount equals $10
  definition i.interest_reports equals [r1.report]
  definition i.has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts equals true
  definition i.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition i.agi equals $0
  definition i.flow_has_seen_deductions equals false
  assertion i.requires_schedule_b
  assertion i.interest_income = $10
```

No reports at all: nothing required, zeros.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNoReports:
  output ok condition
  i scope Interest.Interest

scope TestNoReports:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition i.interest_reports equals []
  definition i.has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts equals false
  definition i.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition i.agi equals $0
  definition i.flow_has_seen_deductions equals false
  assertion not i.requires_schedule_b
  assertion i.interest_income = $0
  assertion i.tax_exempt_interest = $0
  assertion i.total_tax_withheld = $0
  assertion not i.has_interest_income
  assertion not i.unsupported
```

## Box 3, no-1099 interest, tax-exempt interest and withholding

A report with a 1099-INT adds box 3 to box 1 and counts box 8 and box 4. A
report without a 1099-INT uses only its own amount and ignores boxes 3, 4, 6
and 8.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestBoxesAndNo1099:
  output ok condition
  i scope Interest.Interest

scope TestBoxesAndNo1099:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition i.interest_reports equals
    [ Interest.InterestReport {
        -- filer: Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler
        -- has_1099: true
        -- no_1099_amount: $999
        -- writable_1099_amount: $100.20
        -- writable_early_withdrawl_penalty_amount: $0
        -- writable_interest_on_government_bonds: $50.40
        -- writable_tax_withheld: $12.50
        -- writable_foreign_tax_paid: $0
        -- writable_tax_exempt_interest: $20.50
        -- writable_specified_private_activity_bond_interest: $0
        -- writable_market_discount: $0
        -- writable_bond_premium: $0
        -- writable_bond_premium_on_treasury_obligations: $0
        -- writable_bond_premium_on_tax_exempt_bond: $0
        -- state_is_different_state: false
        -- writable_state_tax_withheld: $0
        -- facta_filing_required: false
      };
      Interest.InterestReport {
        -- filer: Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler
        -- has_1099: false
        -- no_1099_amount: $30.10
        -- writable_1099_amount: $7
        -- writable_early_withdrawl_penalty_amount: $0
        -- writable_interest_on_government_bonds: $7
        -- writable_tax_withheld: $7
        -- writable_foreign_tax_paid: $7
        -- writable_tax_exempt_interest: $7
        -- writable_specified_private_activity_bond_interest: $0
        -- writable_market_discount: $0
        -- writable_bond_premium: $0
        -- writable_bond_premium_on_treasury_obligations: $0
        -- writable_bond_premium_on_tax_exempt_bond: $0
        -- state_is_different_state: false
        -- writable_state_tax_withheld: $0
        -- facta_filing_required: false
      } ]
  definition i.has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts equals false
  definition i.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition i.agi equals $0
  definition i.flow_has_seen_deductions equals false
  # not over $1,500: raw sum 100.20 + 50.40 + 30.10 = 180.70, rounded $181
  assertion not i.requires_schedule_b
  assertion i.interest_income = $181
  # line 2a: only the first report's box 8, $20.50 rounds to $21
  assertion i.tax_exempt_interest = $21
  # line 25b part: box 4 $12.50 rounds to $13, the second report gives $0
  assertion i.total_tax_withheld = $13
  # the first report has box 8 different from $0, so the filer is knocked out
  assertion i.ko_flow_knockout_tax_exempt_interest
  assertion i.unsupported
```

## Knockouts

One test per knockout. Each report is the same except for the field named.

```catala
declaration scope KnockoutCase:
  input penalty content money
  input bonds content money
  input foreign_tax content money
  input state_tax content money
  input different_state content boolean
  input facta content boolean
  input interest content money
  input status content Types.FilingStatus
  input agi_in content money
  input seen_deductions content boolean
  output result content Interest.Interest

scope KnockoutCase:
  definition result equals
    output of Interest.Interest with {
      -- interest_reports:
        [ Interest.InterestReport {
          -- filer: Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler
          -- has_1099: true
          -- no_1099_amount: $0
          -- writable_1099_amount: interest
          -- writable_early_withdrawl_penalty_amount: penalty
          -- writable_interest_on_government_bonds: $0
          -- writable_tax_withheld: $0
          -- writable_foreign_tax_paid: foreign_tax
          -- writable_tax_exempt_interest: $0
          -- writable_specified_private_activity_bond_interest: bonds
          -- writable_market_discount: $0
          -- writable_bond_premium: $0
          -- writable_bond_premium_on_treasury_obligations: $0
          -- writable_bond_premium_on_tax_exempt_bond: $0
          -- state_is_different_state: different_state
          -- writable_state_tax_withheld: state_tax
          -- facta_filing_required: facta
        } ]
      -- has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts: false
      -- filing_status: status
      -- agi: agi_in
      -- flow_has_seen_deductions: seen_deductions
    }
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestKnockoutEarlyWithdrawlPenalty:
  output ok condition
  k scope KnockoutCase

scope TestKnockoutEarlyWithdrawlPenalty:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition k.penalty equals $5
  definition k.bonds equals $0
  definition k.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition k.state_tax equals $0
  definition k.different_state equals false
  definition k.facta equals false
  definition k.interest equals $100
  definition k.status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition k.agi_in equals $50,000
  definition k.seen_deductions equals true
  assertion k.result.ko_flow_knockout_has_early_withdrawl_penalty
  assertion k.result.unsupported
  assertion not k.result.ko_flow_knockout_has_bonds
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestKnockoutBonds:
  output ok condition
  k scope KnockoutCase

scope TestKnockoutBonds:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition k.penalty equals $0
  definition k.bonds equals $1
  definition k.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition k.state_tax equals $0
  definition k.different_state equals false
  definition k.facta equals false
  definition k.interest equals $100
  definition k.status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition k.agi_in equals $50,000
  definition k.seen_deductions equals true
  assertion k.result.ko_flow_knockout_has_bonds
  assertion k.result.unsupported
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestKnockoutForeignTax:
  output ok condition
  k scope KnockoutCase

scope TestKnockoutForeignTax:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition k.penalty equals $0
  definition k.bonds equals $0
  definition k.foreign_tax equals $2
  definition k.state_tax equals $0
  definition k.different_state equals false
  definition k.facta equals false
  definition k.interest equals $100
  definition k.status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition k.agi_in equals $50,000
  definition k.seen_deductions equals true
  assertion k.result.ko_flow_knockout_has_foreign_tax_paid
  assertion k.result.unsupported
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestKnockoutStateTaxAndDifferentState:
  output ok condition
  k scope KnockoutCase
  k2 scope KnockoutCase

scope TestKnockoutStateTaxAndDifferentState:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition k.penalty equals $0
  definition k.bonds equals $0
  definition k.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition k.state_tax equals $3
  definition k.different_state equals false
  definition k.facta equals false
  definition k.interest equals $100
  definition k.status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition k.agi_in equals $50,000
  definition k.seen_deductions equals true
  assertion k.result.ko_flow_knockout_state_tax_withheld
  assertion not k.result.ko_flow_knockout_withholding_unsupported_state
  assertion k.result.unsupported
  definition k2.penalty equals $0
  definition k2.bonds equals $0
  definition k2.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition k2.state_tax equals $0
  definition k2.different_state equals true
  definition k2.facta equals false
  definition k2.interest equals $100
  definition k2.status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition k2.agi_in equals $50,000
  definition k2.seen_deductions equals true
  assertion k2.result.ko_flow_knockout_withholding_unsupported_state
  assertion not k2.result.ko_flow_knockout_state_tax_withheld
  assertion k2.result.unsupported
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestKnockoutFacta:
  output ok condition
  k scope KnockoutCase

scope TestKnockoutFacta:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition k.penalty equals $0
  definition k.bonds equals $0
  definition k.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition k.state_tax equals $0
  definition k.different_state equals false
  definition k.facta equals true
  definition k.interest equals $100
  definition k.status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition k.agi_in equals $50,000
  definition k.seen_deductions equals true
  assertion k.result.ko_has_required_facta_filings
  assertion k.result.unsupported
```

A clean filer is not knocked out (the hypotheses of the knockout tests are
satisfiable, and the spec rejects them only when a trigger is present).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNoKnockout:
  output ok condition
  k scope KnockoutCase

scope TestNoKnockout:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition k.penalty equals $0
  definition k.bonds equals $0
  definition k.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition k.state_tax equals $0
  definition k.different_state equals false
  definition k.facta equals false
  definition k.interest equals $100
  definition k.status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition k.agi_in equals $50,000
  definition k.seen_deductions equals true
  assertion not k.result.unsupported
```

## AGI thresholds (NIIT-style knockouts)

IRC 1411(b): $200,000 (single, head of household), $250,000 (joint,
qualifying surviving spouse), $125,000 (separate). The knockout needs interest
income above $0, AGI strictly above the threshold, and the deductions screens
seen.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNiitThresholds:
  output ok condition
  s_at scope KnockoutCase
  s_over scope KnockoutCase
  s_unseen scope KnockoutCase
  j_over scope KnockoutCase
  j_at scope KnockoutCase
  m_over scope KnockoutCase
  m_at scope KnockoutCase
  h_over scope KnockoutCase
  q_over scope KnockoutCase
  s_nointerest scope KnockoutCase

scope TestNiitThresholds:
  rule ok fulfilled
  # single, AGI exactly at the threshold: not over, no knockout
  definition s_at.penalty equals $0
  definition s_at.bonds equals $0
  definition s_at.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition s_at.state_tax equals $0
  definition s_at.different_state equals false
  definition s_at.facta equals false
  definition s_at.status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition s_at.agi_in equals $200,000
  definition s_at.interest equals $100
  definition s_at.seen_deductions equals true
  # single, $1 over: knocked out
  definition s_over.penalty equals $0
  definition s_over.bonds equals $0
  definition s_over.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition s_over.state_tax equals $0
  definition s_over.different_state equals false
  definition s_over.facta equals false
  definition s_over.status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition s_over.agi_in equals $200,001
  definition s_over.interest equals $100
  definition s_over.seen_deductions equals true
  # same but deductions not yet seen: not knocked out
  definition s_unseen.penalty equals $0
  definition s_unseen.bonds equals $0
  definition s_unseen.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition s_unseen.state_tax equals $0
  definition s_unseen.different_state equals false
  definition s_unseen.facta equals false
  definition s_unseen.status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition s_unseen.agi_in equals $200,001
  definition s_unseen.interest equals $100
  definition s_unseen.seen_deductions equals false
  # MFJ
  definition j_over.penalty equals $0
  definition j_over.bonds equals $0
  definition j_over.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition j_over.state_tax equals $0
  definition j_over.different_state equals false
  definition j_over.facta equals false
  definition j_over.status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition j_over.agi_in equals $250,001
  definition j_over.interest equals $100
  definition j_over.seen_deductions equals true
  definition j_at.penalty equals $0
  definition j_at.bonds equals $0
  definition j_at.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition j_at.state_tax equals $0
  definition j_at.different_state equals false
  definition j_at.facta equals false
  definition j_at.status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition j_at.agi_in equals $250,000
  definition j_at.interest equals $100
  definition j_at.seen_deductions equals true
  # MFS
  definition m_over.penalty equals $0
  definition m_over.bonds equals $0
  definition m_over.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition m_over.state_tax equals $0
  definition m_over.different_state equals false
  definition m_over.facta equals false
  definition m_over.status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition m_over.agi_in equals $125,001
  definition m_over.interest equals $100
  definition m_over.seen_deductions equals true
  definition m_at.penalty equals $0
  definition m_at.bonds equals $0
  definition m_at.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition m_at.state_tax equals $0
  definition m_at.different_state equals false
  definition m_at.facta equals false
  definition m_at.status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition m_at.agi_in equals $125,000
  definition m_at.interest equals $100
  definition m_at.seen_deductions equals true
  # head of household uses the single threshold, QSS the joint one
  definition h_over.penalty equals $0
  definition h_over.bonds equals $0
  definition h_over.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition h_over.state_tax equals $0
  definition h_over.different_state equals false
  definition h_over.facta equals false
  definition h_over.status equals Types.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold
  definition h_over.agi_in equals $200,001
  definition h_over.interest equals $100
  definition h_over.seen_deductions equals true
  definition q_over.penalty equals $0
  definition q_over.bonds equals $0
  definition q_over.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition q_over.state_tax equals $0
  definition q_over.different_state equals false
  definition q_over.facta equals false
  definition q_over.status equals Types.FilingStatus.QualifyingSurvivingSpouse
  definition q_over.agi_in equals $250,001
  definition q_over.interest equals $100
  definition q_over.seen_deductions equals true
  # no interest income: no knockout whatever the AGI
  definition s_nointerest.penalty equals $0
  definition s_nointerest.bonds equals $0
  definition s_nointerest.foreign_tax equals $0
  definition s_nointerest.state_tax equals $0
  definition s_nointerest.different_state equals false
  definition s_nointerest.facta equals false
  definition s_nointerest.status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition s_nointerest.agi_in equals $900,000
  definition s_nointerest.interest equals $0
  definition s_nointerest.seen_deductions equals true
  assertion not s_at.result.unsupported
  assertion s_over.result.ko_has_interest_income_and_agi_above_threshold_for_single_or_hoh
  assertion s_over.result.unsupported
  assertion not s_unseen.result.unsupported
  assertion j_over.result.ko_has_interest_income_and_agi_above_threshold_for_mfj_or_qss
  assertion not j_at.result.unsupported
  assertion m_over.result.ko_has_interest_income_and_agi_above_threshold_for_mfs
  assertion not m_at.result.unsupported
  assertion h_over.result.ko_has_interest_income_and_agi_above_threshold_for_single_or_hoh
  assertion q_over.result.ko_has_interest_income_and_agi_above_threshold_for_mfj_or_qss
  assertion not s_nointerest.result.unsupported
```
